{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975784,"nonce":"a0kv7i7l7OdGj1BFQCNn3uw5Rr4=","title":"Carry the AirConfigKey with an OSR entry and compare it at the transfer","message":"What enforces the OSR configuration invariant today is that every producer\nremembers to call `interpreter_config_for`. The existing guard records the\nproducer's key and refuses a mismatched transfer, but a real divergence stops the\npcs matching first, so OSR is lost silently rather than taken wrongly -- it\ncatches the pc-collision case only.\n\nUnenforced cases, roughly by likelihood of biting:\n  - hot reload runs a second level (O3 -\u003e O2 plus callees hidden) while OSR\n    bodies for the same findex stay at `interpreter_config_for`'s level;\n  - Cranelift re-tier slots come from the ordinary compile's `Optimized` and are\n    re-mapped onto the OSR compile's `block_pcs`, safe only because a function\n    with a re-tier site has a back edge;\n  - four CLI diagnostics and `report_hot_loop` hardcode O2, so `osr_report`\n    answers at a level no consumer runs.\n\nFix: carry the key with the entry and compare it where the transfer is decided.","files":null}]}